@page "/tower"
@using RavenNest.Combat
@inject RavenNest.BusinessLogic.Game.TowerManager TowerManager

@*
    The tower (the game's docs/tower-design.md section 6 and docs/tower-worlds-proposal.md section 12): the floors some
    stream has reached, each a world with its town, and the floor's parts with their objectives, their guardian and
    the level they are made for, who cleared them first, and the streams that have climbed highest (by floor, then by
    part). Floors and parts nobody has reached stay hidden (no spoilers, Zerratar 2026-11-07): they show once a stream
    gets there, and a floor's boss is named only once its last part is reached. Everything is read from
    RavenNest.Combat.Tower, the same list the game and the server use; the server counts in steps and Tower maps them
    to floors and parts.
*@
<div class="top-section">
    <div class="hero-text">
        <h1>The tower</h1>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="white-section-break"></div>
<div class="page-content">
    <div class="section rf-tower">
        <p class="rf-lead">
            A climb the whole stream makes together. The tower has <b>floors</b>, each a world of its own with a town,
            and every floor has <b>parts</b>. Type <b>!tower</b> to go to the part your stream is on and fight its
            monsters; the players who stay behind keep training as usual. Every part has <b>objectives</b> for the whole
            stream, and all of them count by themselves while you play: its monsters defeated, materials the stream's
            players gather wherever they train, hidden things found by whoever trains near them. When they are done, the
            part's <b>guardian</b> can be challenged with <b>!tower boss</b>: the streamer or a moderator starts it, or
            any player in the tower votes for it (it starts a minute later, or at once when most of the players who are
            there vote too), and everyone has a minute to join. Most guardians are <b>mini bosses</b>; the guardian of a
            floor's last part is the <b>floor boss</b>, and beating it opens the next floor and its town.
        </p>
        <p class="rf-tower__rules">
            <b>Level sync:</b> on a part everyone fights as if at most a tenth above the part's level: skill levels, health
            and gear count only up to that, while skill trees, gems, crits and elements count in full. A stream of veterans
            climbs the same tower as a new one.
            <b>The fights follow the group:</b> a part is made for @Tower.SuggestedGroup players, a floor boss for @Tower.FloorBossGroup. With more in the fight, or
            with players made stronger by their skill trees and gems, its monsters and guardians have more health, a
            guardian calls more helpers and hits a little harder; a smaller group meets a smaller fight. The first floor
            follows the group only a little, every floor above it more.
            A boss attempt lasts at most @(Tower.BossTimeLimitSeconds / 60) minutes. Whoever falls is out of the attempt;
            if everyone falls, the stream regroups for @(Tower.BossRetrySeconds / 60) minutes before the next try.
            Whoever lands the last blow on a floor boss earns a title.
            A floor, and each of its parts, stays a mystery until some stream reaches it.
            <b>Climbing pays:</b> on a part your combat skills and Healing never earn less than they would on your
            island (a boss fight, its countdown, getting back up and the walk to the next monster included), and every
            floor gives @((int)Math.Round(Tower.ExpPerFloor * 100))% more on top: @((int)Math.Round(Tower.ExpBonus(1) * 100))% on the first floor, @((int)Math.Round(Tower.ExpBonus(3) * 100))% on the third.
            The towns pay what your island does.
        </p>
        <p class="rf-tower__rules">
            <b>In chat:</b> <b>!tower</b> goes in, <b>!tower info</b> says where the stream is, <b>!tower boss</b> challenges
            the guardian, <b>!tower climb</b> goes on up from the town, <b>!tower town</b> goes to the floor's town,
            <b>!tower part 3</b> takes you to a part already cleared to train there (<b>!tower 1-3</b> names the floor
            too, <b>!tower floor 1</b> goes to a floor's latest part), <b>!tower leave</b> takes only you out and
            <b>!tower close</b> ends the climb for now.
        </p>
        <p class="rf-tower__rules">
            <b>Cleared parts stay open:</b> once your stream has cleared a part, any player can go back there to train,
            like sailing to an island, while the climb goes on elsewhere: <b>!tower part 3</b> takes only you (to a part
            of the floor you are on; <b>!tower 1-3</b> names the floor too), and <b>!tower</b> brings you back to the
            climb. Up to three parts are open at once: the climb's, and two more that whoever asks first opens; a part
            nobody is on closes again after a while. The streamer or a vote can still take the climbing group along with
            <b>!tower all part 3</b>, and back with <b>!tower all</b> (players on a part of their own stay there).
            <b>!tower boss now</b> lets the streamer or a moderator skip a boss countdown. In a boss fight a knocked
            out player recovers by the entrance and comes back into the fight. <b>!tower map</b> shows the floor's map in the game.
            <b>A small stream is not a slow one:</b> a monster defeated counts for more toward a part's objectives when
            few players are on the part and for less when many are, so two players need well under twice the time of
            five, and thirty are fast without being done in minutes.
        </p>

        @foreach (var band in Tower.Bands.Where(b => b.FirstFloor <= revealed))
        {
            var town = Tower.Towns.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Band == band.Number);
            var bossStep = band.LastFloor;
            var bossFirst = firsts.TryGetValue(bossStep, out var bf) ? bf : null;
            <h2 class="rf-tower__band" style="--element: @ElementColor(band.Element)">Floor @band.Number: @band.Name</h2>
            <div class="rf-tower__bandinfo">
                <p>@band.Description</p>
                <div class="rf-badges">
                    <span class="rf-badge">@band.Parts parts</span>
                    <span class="rf-badge">Levels @Tower.Level(band.FirstFloor) to @Tower.Level(band.LastFloor)</span>
                    <span class="rf-badge">+@((int)Math.Round(Tower.ExpBonus(band.Number) * 100))% experience</span>
                    <span class="rf-badge" style="--element: @ElementColor(band.Element)">Its monsters strike with @band.Element.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()</span>
                    @foreach (var weak in Weaknesses(band.Resistance))
                    {
                        <span class="rf-badge rf-badge--good">Weak to @weak</span>
                    }
                    @foreach (var strong in Resists(band.Resistance))
                    {
                        <span class="rf-badge rf-badge--warn">Resists @strong</span>
                    }
                </div>
                @if (bossFirst != null)
                {
                    <p class="rf-tower__worldfirst">
                        <span class="rf-tower__firstlabel">World first</span>
                        <b>@bossFirst.Name</b> beat the floor boss, @Tower.Get(bossStep).Boss.Name, first, on
                        <span title="@bossFirst.Cleared.ToString("f")">@bossFirst.Cleared.ToString("d MMM yyyy")</span>
                        with @bossFirst.Players @(bossFirst.Players == 1 ? "player" : "players")@(bossFirst.LastHitBy != null ? ". The last blow was " + bossFirst.LastHitBy + "'s" : "").
                    </p>
                }
            </div>

            @* the floor as a map: its town, its areas and their parts, lit as far as any stream has got *@
            <TowerFloorMap Floor="band.Number" ClearedThrough="clearedThrough" Reached="revealed" ClimbWord="The furthest any stream has climbed" />

            @if (town != null)
            {
                <div class="rf-card rf-tower__town">
                    <h3 class="rf-card__title">The town of @town.Name</h3>
                    <p class="rf-tower__text">@town.Description Type <b>!tower town</b> to go there, and <b>!tower talk</b> to
                        hear what its people have to say. Most of them have a quest chain of their own for every player, with a
                        reward found nowhere else, and some ask the whole stream for help with a part of the floor. After every
                        cleared part everyone goes down to the town to rest and train; <b>!tower climb</b> takes everyone up to
                        the next part. A town further down needs its name: <b>!tower town mossgate</b>.</p>
                    <ul class="rf-tower__people">
                        @foreach (var npc in town.People)
                        {
                            <li><b>@npc.Name</b><span class="rf-table__quiet">@npc.Role</span></li>
                        }
                    </ul>
                </div>
            }

            <ol class="rf-tower__floors">
                @foreach (var part in Tower.Floors.Where(f => f.Number >= band.FirstFloor && f.Number <= band.LastFloor && f.Number <= revealed))
                {
                    var first = firsts.TryGetValue(part.Number, out var f) ? f : null;
                    <li class="rf-card rf-tower__floor@(part.IsFloorBoss ? " rf-tower__floor--milestone" : "")">
                        <div class="rf-tower__number" title="@part.Label">@part.Part</div>
                        <div class="rf-tower__body">
                            <h3 class="rf-card__title">@part.Name <span class="rf-tower__place">@part.Label</span></h3>
                            <p class="rf-tower__text">@part.Description</p>
                            <div class="rf-tower__facts">
                                <span><b>Made for</b> combat level @part.Level, @part.GroupSize players@(Tower.BossGroup(part) != part.GroupSize ? ", its boss for " + Tower.BossGroup(part) : "") (synced to level @Tower.SyncLevel(part.Number))</span>
                            </div>
                            <ul class="rf-tower__objectives">
                                @foreach (var q in part.Objectives)
                                {
                                    <li class="rf-tower__objective rf-tower__objective--@q.Kind.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()">
                                        <span class="rf-tower__kind">@KindName(q, part)</span>
                                        <span class="rf-tower__what">
                                            <b>@q.Text</b>
                                            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(q.Story))
                                            {
                                                <span class="rf-tower__note">@q.Story</span>
                                            }
                                            @if (q.Kind == TowerObjectiveKind.Gather)
                                            {
                                                <span class="rf-tower__note">Counts what the stream's players gather with @Skills(q), wherever they train (nothing is taken from anyone), and every monster defeated on this part.</span>
                                            }
                                            else if (q.Kind == TowerObjectiveKind.Find)
                                            {
                                                <span class="rf-tower__note">Hidden on this part. Whoever trains near one finds it after a while.</span>
                                            }
                                            else if (q.Kind == TowerObjectiveKind.Guardian)
                                            {
                                                <span class="rf-tower__note">@(part.IsFloorBoss ? "Opens when the part's other objectives are done. Beating it clears the floor." : "Opens when the part's other objectives are done.")</span>
                                            }
                                        </span>
                                    </li>
                                }
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="rf-tower__first">
                            @if (first != null)
                            {
                                <span class="rf-tower__firstlabel">@(part.IsFloorBoss ? "World first" : "First clear")</span>
                                <b>@first.Name</b>
                                <span class="rf-table__quiet" title="@first.Cleared.ToString("f")">@first.Cleared.ToString("d MMM yyyy")</span>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <span class="rf-table__quiet">Not cleared by anyone yet</span>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </li>
                }
            </ol>
            @if (band.LastFloor > revealed)
            {
                var from = Tower.PartOf(revealed) + 1;
                <div class="rf-card rf-tower__hidden">
                    <span class="rf-tower__number">?</span>
                    <p>@(from == band.Parts ? "Part " + from : "Parts " + from + " to " + band.Parts) of floor @band.Number
                        @(from == band.Parts ? "is" : "are") still hidden, and so is the floor's boss: no stream has got
                        that far yet. Clear part @Tower.PartOf(revealed) to see what waits beyond.</p>
                </div>
            }
        }
        @if (Tower.Bands.Any(b => b.FirstFloor > revealed))
        {
            <p class="rf-table__quiet">More floors lie above, unseen.</p>
        }

        <h2 class="rf-tower__band">The highest climbs</h2>
        @if (leaders.Count == 0)
        {
            <p class="rf-table__quiet">No stream has cleared a part yet. Be the first.</p>
        }
        else
        {
            <table class="rf-table rf-table--stack rf-tower__leaders">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col" class="rf-table__num">#</th>
                        <th scope="col">Stream</th>
                        <th scope="col">Highest part cleared</th>
                        <th scope="col" class="rf-table__num">Floors cleared</th>
                        <th scope="col">When</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    @for (var i = 0; i < leaders.Count; i++)
                    {
                        var l = leaders[i];
                        <tr>
                            <td class="rf-table__num" data-label="#">@(i + 1)</td>
                            <td data-label="Stream"><b>@l.Name</b></td>
                            <td data-label="Highest part">Floor @l.Floor, part @l.Part</td>
                            <td class="rf-table__num" data-label="Floors cleared">@l.FloorsCleared</td>
                            <td class="rf-table__quiet" data-label="When" title="@l.Cleared.ToString("f")">@l.Cleared.ToString("d MMM yyyy")</td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                </tbody>
            </table>
        }
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    private int revealed = 1;
    // the highest step some stream has cleared (the parts up to it are lit on the floor maps)
    private int clearedThrough;
    private IReadOnlyDictionary<int, RavenNest.BusinessLogic.Game.TowerManager.FirstClear> firsts = new Dictionary<int, RavenNest.BusinessLogic.Game.TowerManager.FirstClear>();
    private IReadOnlyList<RavenNest.BusinessLogic.Game.TowerManager.Leader> leaders = new List<RavenNest.BusinessLogic.Game.TowerManager.Leader>();

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        revealed = TowerManager.Revealed();
        firsts = TowerManager.FirstClears();
        clearedThrough = firsts.Count > 0 ? firsts.Keys.Max() : 0;
        leaders = TowerManager.Leaderboard(25);
    }

    private static string KindName(TowerObjective q, TowerFloorDefinition part) => q.Kind switch
    {
        TowerObjectiveKind.Kill => "Monsters",
        TowerObjectiveKind.Gather => "Materials",
        TowerObjectiveKind.Find => "Hidden",
        TowerObjectiveKind.Guardian => part.IsFloorBoss ? "Floor boss" : "Mini boss",
        _ => "",
    };

    private static string Skills(TowerObjective q) =>
        q.Skills.Length <= 1 ? string.Join("", q.Skills) : string.Join(", ", q.Skills.Take(q.Skills.Length - 1)) + " or " + q.Skills[q.Skills.Length - 1];

    private static string ElementColor(Element e) => e switch
    {
        Element.Fire => "#ff7a59",
        Element.Ice => "#6ec6ff",
        Element.Lightning => "#ffd166",
        Element.Poison => "#8fdc5a",
        _ => "#c9c3b6",
    };

    private static IEnumerable<string> Weaknesses(ElementValues r) => Each(r).Where(x => x.Value < 0).Select(x => x.Name);
    private static IEnumerable<string> Resists(ElementValues r) => Each(r).Where(x => x.Value > 0).Select(x => x.Name);

    private static IEnumerable<(string Name, double Value)> Each(ElementValues r)
    {
        yield return ("fire", r.Fire);
        yield return ("ice", r.Ice);
        yield return ("lightning", r.Lightning);
        yield return ("poison", r.Poison);
    }
}
